# fieldtest sources — real-world MATLAB projects, one per line:
#   <git-url>  |  <license>  |  <what it exercises>
# Policy: permissive licenses only (MIT/BSD/Apache-2.0). Cloned into the
# gitignored corpus/ by fetch.py — never committed.

# ── ML / neural networks (classic APIs: mapminmax, newff, train, sim) ──────
https://github.com/rasmusbergpalm/DeepLearnToolbox.git       | BSD-2-Clause | classic deep-learning (NN/CNN/DBN/SAE): matrix math, .mat data round-trips
https://github.com/PRML/PRMLT.git                            | MIT | Bishop PRML algorithms: linear models, SVM, EM, graphical models
https://github.com/trekhleb/machine-learning-octave.git      | MIT | popular ML algorithms as annotated examples (Octave/MATLAB dialect)
https://github.com/Borye/machine-learning-coursera-1.git     | MIT | Andrew Ng's ML course exercises (the canonical real-world learner corpus)
https://github.com/vkosuri/CourseraMachineLearning.git       | MIT | same course, independent port — cross-checks the other copy
https://github.com/albanie/convnet-burden.git                | MIT | convnet memory/FLOP estimates: table math, file sweeps

# ── Signal / image processing (FFT-heavy, matrices as data) ────────────────
https://github.com/morriswmz/doa-tools.git                   | MIT | direction-of-arrival estimation: MUSIC/ESPRIT/beamforming, array math
https://github.com/WenzheLiu-Speech/sound-source-localization-algorithm_DOA_estimation.git | Apache-2.0 | DOA/SRP speech localization — Chinese DSP corpus
https://github.com/joeyos/SAR-imaging.git                    | Apache-2.0 | synthetic-aperture radar imaging: heavy FFT/convolution numerics
https://github.com/Aiwiscal/ECG-ML-DL-Algorithm-Matlab.git   | Apache-2.0 | ECG filtering/QRS detection — biomedical DSP
https://github.com/robbystk/emg.git                          | MIT | electromyography signal processing functions
https://github.com/google/ffcc.git                           | Apache-2.0 | Google's Fast Fourier Color Constancy — numeric ML on images

# ── Optimization / control / simulation (ODEs, solvers) ───────────────────
https://github.com/OpenOCL/OpenOCL.git                       | BSD-3-Clause | optimal control library: trajectory optimization, ODE constraints
https://github.com/deng-haoyang/ParNMPC.git                  | BSD-2-Clause | nonlinear model-predictive control toolkit
https://github.com/kaichen686/GINav.git                      | BSD-2-Clause | GNSS/INS integration: Kalman filtering, geodesy
https://github.com/cybergalactic/MSS.git                     | MIT | marine systems simulator: hydrodynamics, control (pure-.m parts)
https://github.com/MultiDIC/MultiDIC.git                     | Apache-2.0 | digital image correlation: calibration, stereo, numerics

# ── Metaheuristics / operations research ───────────────────────────────────
https://github.com/alpsayin/genetic-algorithm-matlab.git     | MIT | minimal clean GA implementation
https://github.com/izzuddinafif/MATLAB-GA-PSO.git            | MIT | hybrid GA + PSO optimization
https://github.com/LenKerr/matlab-tsp-ga.git                 | MIT | TSP/MTSP via GA
https://github.com/OLPS/OLPS.git                             | Apache-2.0 | online portfolio selection: 20+ numeric strategies

# ── Math modeling / educational breadth (largest script diversity) ────────
https://github.com/HuangCongQing/Algorithms_MathModels.git   | MIT | math-modeling algorithms: AHP, TSP, GA/PSO, classic NN textbook code (Chinese comments, GBK encoding — exercises the transcode path)
https://github.com/ravenxrz/Mathematical-Modeling.git        | Apache-2.0 | math modeling course corpus (Chinese)
https://github.com/Gagniuc/MATLAB-Coding-Examples-from-Simple-to-Complex.git | MIT | book code: basics → graphs → advanced, wide API surface

# ── Quants / risk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
https://github.com/TommasoBelluzzo/SystemicRisk.git          | Apache-2.0 | financial systemic-risk framework: stats + econometrics

# ── Data serialization (structs/cells/strings torture, no display) ────────
https://github.com/NeuroJSON/jsonlab.git                     | BSD-3-Clause | JSON load/save in pure MATLAB: structs/cells/strings torture

# NOTE: graphics/display repos (export_fig, matlab2tikz, ZoomPlot, …) are
# deliberately EXCLUDED for now — the current phase is compute/processing
# only. A later graphics phase will add them back.
